(vector (map (:adr/related (vector "2607160005-kotoba-fleet-vcs-plane" "2607170500-kagi-vault-cloud-persistence-fleet-key-rotation")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/id "2607178000"), (:adr/context "ADR-2607170500 restored fleet signing keys and asked (owner 「次」→「do it」) to extend fleet-native CI from a single manual demo receipt (org-spirit-in-physics-comics docs-check only, kagami/nekko/bonsai/kotoba-delta present as pin-reachability only) into real, recurring test execution on murakumo compute. Gap audit found: (1) kagami/nekko/bonsai/kotoba-delta had no actual gate beyond pin-reachability, (2) no murakumo node had a working JVM/clojure toolchain by default (zebulun has openjdk+clojure via homebrew but JAVA_HOME unset; asher/others have neither), (3) no scheduled trigger existed — the one working receipt was a manual one-off, (4) RemoteTrigger (claude.ai routine mechanism) requires a pre-configured environment_id/self_hosted_runner_pool_id not present for this repo. Owner chose (AskUserQuestion) full automation via a newly-issued, narrowly-scoped signing key rather than deploying fleet-owner-key or leaving automation manual."), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/helpers (vector "~/.gftd/run-fleet-ci-murakumo-tick.cljs" "~/.gftd/fleet-ci-gates/gate-jvm-test.cljs" "~/.gftd/fleet-ci-gates/gate-nbb-test.cljs" "~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.gftd.fleet-ci-murakumo-tick.plist")), (:adr/exit-criteria "{:gates-beyond-pin-reachable 5, :standing-runner-installed true, :signer-has-zero-governance-grant true}"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607178000: fleet-native CI standing runner — real gates on murakumo + narrow-scope automation key\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-17\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (owner「gap を埋めて」; AskUserQuestion selection「専用の弱権限キーを新規発行して完全自動化」)\n**Related**: ADR-2607160005 (kotoba-fleet-vcs plane, native CI receipt design), ADR-2607170500 (kagi vault cloud persistence + fleet key rotation)\n\n## Context\n\nA prior session step landed one signed fleet-ci.edn receipt covering 5 repos\n(kagami/nekko/bonsai/kotoba-delta/org-spirit-in-physics-comics), but only\norg-spirit-in-physics-comics had a REAL gate (a doc-EDN validator on asher);\nthe other 4 only had `pin-reachable` checks (GitHub reachability, not test\nexecution). GitHub Actions `.github/workflows/ci.yml` remained the only place\nactually running `clojure -M:test` for nekko/bonsai/kagi. Asked to audit\nremaining gaps, then to fill them.\n\nGap audit (this session) found:\n\n1. **No real gate for kagami/nekko/bonsai/kotoba-delta** — pin-reachability\n   only, not test execution.\n2. **No murakumo node had a ready JVM+clojure toolchain**: `asher` has\n   node/npm/nbb but no java. Of 9 mesh nodes probed (naphtali, simeon, judah,\n   zebulun, levi, joseph, issachar, dan, benjamin), only **zebulun** has both\n   `clojure` (homebrew) and a JDK (openjdk@26, homebrew) — but `/usr/bin/java`\n   is the unconfigured macOS stub, so `JAVA_HOME=/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk`\n   must be set per-invocation (no system-wide java symlink was touched).\n3. **GitHub Actions still runs in parallel**, unreplaced — nekko/bonsai/kagi\n   `ci.yml` still execute `clojure -M:test` on every push. This ADR is\n   additive (murakumo now ALSO verifies), not a GitHub Actions migration —\n   disabling those workflows is a separate decision with branch-protection\n   implications, out of scope here.\n4. **No automated trigger** — the existing receipt was a one-off manual\n   `fleet ci-verify` invocation. `RemoteTrigger` (the mechanism behind\n   `itonami-react-growth-hourly` / `bmc-business-operate-daily`) needs a\n   pre-configured `environment_id` or `self_hosted_runner_pool_id`; neither\n   exists for this repo under the current account, and `list` returned zero\n   existing triggers — creating one blind was declined in favor of asking.\n5. **kagitaba \"cloud sync\" gap, reassessed as mischaracterized**: kagitaba\n   (`kotoba-lang/kagitaba`) is a zero-dependency `.cljc` DATA MODEL library\n   (category/field/item taxonomy) with no storage layer of its own — kagi\n   consumes kagitaba items, pr-str's them, encrypts, and stores them in the\n   kagi vault. There is no separate \"kagitaba vault\" to sync; kagi's existing\n   whole-vault `push!`/`pull!` (ADR-2607170500) already covers every kagitaba\n   item transitively. The real, smaller residual gap is ADR-2607170500's own\n   follow-up (a): push/pull operate at vault granularity, not per-item — left\n   as a documented future enhancement, not a functional defect.\n\nAsked the owner how to design recurring automation given the signing-key\nplacement question (gate collection is safe to automate, but WHO can\nunattended-sign a receipt is a real security decision — this is the exact\nclass of carelessness that caused the fleet-owner-key loss in ADR-2607170500).\nOwner selected: **issue a dedicated weak-privilege key and fully automate**.\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. Real gates (not just pin-reachability), verified live before landing\n\n| repo | node | gate | proof (this session) |\n|------|------|------|----|\n| kagami | zebulun | `clojure -M:test` | 18 tests / 107 assertions, 0 failures |\n| nekko | zebulun | `clojure -M:test` | 65 tests / 121 assertions, 0 failures |\n| bonsai | zebulun | `clojure -M:test` | 40 tests / 86 assertions, 0 failures |\n| kotoba-delta | asher | `npx nbb --classpath src:test run-tests.cljs` | 5 tests / 34 assertions, 0 failures |\n| org-spirit-in-physics-comics | asher | doc-EDN tx-data validator (pre-existing) | 78 doc-EDN files valid |\n\nGate driver scripts are nbb (`~/.gftd/fleet-ci-gates/gate-jvm-test.cljs`,\n`gate-nbb-test.cljs`) per the repo's nbb-only script-host rule\n(ADR-2607173000) — no new `.sh`. Each extracts a tarball of the EXACT pinned\ncommit (fetched fresh from GitHub's tarball API, never a local checkout — the\nsame staleness class ADR-2607170500 already flagged) and runs the repo's real\ntest entrypoint.\n\nAs part of this pass, org-spirit-in-physics-comics's west.yml pin was found 2\ncommits stale (`c0868832` vs `origin/main` tip `34c43785`, already the exact\ncommit the existing docs-check gate was built against) and advanced via the\nestablished minimal-single-line-diff GitHub-API PUT pattern.\n\n### 2. Standing runner: `~/.gftd/run-fleet-ci-murakumo-tick.cljs` + LaunchAgent `com.gftd.fleet-ci-murakumo-tick`\n\nFollows the existing house pattern for standing runners (`~/.gftd/run-itonami-qwen36-tick.cljs`\n+ `com.gftd.itonami-qwen36-tick.plist`, ADR-2607172900): nbb script, `StartInterval`\n21600s (6h), `RunAtLoad` false, logs to `~/.gftd/fleet-ci-murakumo-tick.log`.\n\nEach tick: (1) fetches `manifest/west.yml` fresh from GitHub (never the shared\nlocal checkout — this exact drift was observed live during development,\nkagami/nekko/bonsai pins advanced twice mid-session from concurrent activity),\n(2) resolves each of the 5 repos' CURRENT pin, (3) fetches a tarball at that\nexact SHA via GitHub's tarball API, (4) dispatches the corresponding gate to\nzebulun or asher over SSH, (5) invokes `fleet ci-verify --key\n~/.gftd/fleet-ci-signer.pem` to sign a receipt recording all 10 checks\n(5 pin-reachable + 5 gate), (6) lands the new line into\n`com-junkawasaki/root`'s `manifest/fleet-ci.edn` via branch + content-verified\nPUT + server-side merge + branch delete (the same pattern used manually all\nsession — never a direct main push).\n\nScope is deliberately narrow: the SUBJECT of each check is each repo's\nCURRENTLY PINNED commit — a recurring regression check on what the fleet\nalready trusts, not an auto-advance-on-green pipeline. Pin advances remain a\nseparate, deliberately-verified act per the existing manifest workflow\n(ADR-2606272237). Touches only `manifest/fleet-ci.edn`; never `west.yml`,\n`fleet-db.edn`, or any other repo's history.\n\nDry-run verified twice this session — first run observed kagami/nekko/bonsai\npins had already advanced again from a concurrent session mid-development\n(proving the fresh-fetch design correctly tracks live drift instead of\nsigning stale state); second run completed end-to-end unattended: 5/5 gates\npass, receipt signed, landed to `manifest/fleet-ci.edn`, zero manual steps.\n\n### 3. Narrow-scope automation key (not fleet-owner-key)\n\nEnrolled via kagami's existing `fleet enroll` mechanism (designed exactly for\nper-agent scoped identities, ADR-2607160005) rather than inventing a new\nfleet-keys.edn concept:\n\n```\nfleet enroll --agent murakumo-ci --grant \"fleet-ci/*\" --registry manifest/fleet-agents.edn\n```\n\n- kagi name `fleet-agent-murakumo-ci` (compartment personal; cloud-backed via\n  the ADR-2607170500 `kagi push` mechanism like every other kagi item).\n- `did:key:z6MktD3itg4KnsVZZfKX2nTb19JnbzFy5WMCYbgoG4jnRNVw`, appended to\n  `manifest/fleet-agents.edn` (append-only agent registry) with grant\n  `\"fleet-ci/*\"`.\n- **Absent from `fleet-keys.edn`'s `:keys`/`:roots`/`:canonical`** — zero\n  pin-advance authority, zero governance-quorum membership. `fleet.ci`'s\n  `verify-receipt` only checks CID/signature/outcome-consistency against the\n  claimed signer; it is downstream consumers (pin-advance / govern paths) that\n  decide which signer DIDs carry real authority, and this key is deliberately\n  excluded from all of them. A compromised copy can at most forge/spam\n  entries in the append-only `fleet-ci.edn` audit log — it cannot move a pin,\n  pass governance quorum, or touch `fleet-db.edn`/`fleet-head.edn`.\n- Private key material lives ONLY at `~/.gftd/fleet-ci-signer.pem` (mode 600)\n  on the operator's own already-trusted machine, which also runs the\n  orchestrator (fetches pins, dispatches SSH gate runs, lands via `gh`\n  using the operator's own existing GitHub auth). It is never copied to a\n  shared/remote murakumo node — those nodes only ever execute test suites,\n  never see any signing key.\n\n### 4. Deliberately left alone\n\n- GitHub Actions workflows (nekko/bonsai/kagi `ci.yml`) — left running,\n  unreplaced. A real migration/replace decision needs its own ADR (branch\n  protection / required-status-check implications).\n- kagitaba: no code change (see reassessment above) — vault-granularity\n  push/pull sync (ADR-2607170500 follow-up (a)) is a future enhancement, not\n  addressed here.\n- Multi-device concurrent-edit merge semantics (ADR-2607170500 follow-up (b),\n  last-writer-wins) — unchanged, matches the 1Password precedent.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- fleet-ci.edn now carries genuine, recurring, cryptographically-signed\n  evidence that 5 fleet-trust-path repos' real test suites pass on murakumo\n  compute — not GitHub Actions, not a one-off demo.\n- The standing runner's blast radius on compromise is bounded by construction\n  (narrow key, single append-only target file, fresh-pin-only reads).\n- Follow-up candidates (not started): GitHub Actions replacement decision;\n  kagitaba item-granularity sync; extending gate coverage to more west\n  projects; auto-advance-pin-on-green as an explicit, separately-designed\n  opt-in.\n\n## Addendum (2026-07-18): wave-2 repo expansion + false-pass bug fix\n\n**Bug found and fixed**: gate-jvm-test.cljs originally extracted GitHub-tarball-API\narchives without --strip-components=1. That API always wraps content in a\ntop-level <owner>-<repo>-<sha7>/ directory, so `clojure -M:test` ran from a\ndirectory with no deps.edn, silently fell through to a bare Clojure REPL,\nand exited 0 on EOF stdin (closed stdin under nohup/launchd) — a FALSE PASS\nwith the test suite never actually executed. This shipped in the very first\nstanding-runner receipt (manifest/fleet-ci.edn line 5): its\nkagami/nekko/bonsai gate checks are not trustworthy evidence, though their\nouter receipt signature/CID are still valid (the test outcome, not the\nreceipt integrity, was wrong). Root-caused by manually reproducing the exact\nfailure (`clojure -M:test` from an unstripped extraction printed the version\nbanner and exited 0 immediately). Fixed by detecting the wrapper from the\nactual tar listing (do all sampled entries share one top-level directory\nsegment?) rather than assuming either archive shape. Verified the fix against\nboth shapes (git-archive unwrapped, GitHub-tarball-API wrapped) before\nredeploying. The very next tick (line 6, an autonomous LaunchAgent firing —\nnot manually triggered) shows genuine \"Ran 18 tests containing 107\nassertions... 0 failures\" output for kagami, confirming the fix landed before\nany further false passes.\n\n**Coverage expanded from 5 to 14 repos.** Added the direct dependency closure\nof the already-covered repos — kagi's deps (langgraph, kagitaba,\norg-ietf-ed25519, tech-ipfs-specs-ipns) and nekko/bonsai's deps\n(io-multiformats, org-ietf-cbor, io-ipld, chain,\norg-chainagnostic-cacao) — reasoning: these repos' correctness directly\ndetermines whether the already-trusted repos' behavior is trustworthy, so\nverifying one hop of dependency closure meaningfully strengthens the same\ntrust chain rather than being an arbitrary scope expansion. All 9 use the\nidentical deps.edn :test alias shape (cognitect test-runner), so\ngate-jvm-test.cljs needed no changes beyond the wrapper-detection fix.\nrun-fleet-ci-murakumo-tick.cljs was refactored from 5 hardcoded gate\nbindings to a data-driven jvm-repos vector so future expansions are a\none-line change.\n\n**Verified via the real standing runner** (not a manual one-off): a full run\ncovering all 14 repos completed unattended end-to-end — 14 pin-reachability\nchecks + 14 real gate checks (12 JVM clojure -M:test / 1 nbb test suite / 1\ndoc-EDN validator), all 28 :pass, signed with the same narrow-scope\nfleet-agent-murakumo-ci key, landed to manifest/fleet-ci.edn (now 8\nappend-only lines total — the original 5 plus two genuine autonomous\nLaunchAgent firings observed overnight at their 6-hour interval, plus this\nfinal wave-2 receipt).\n\n**Cosmetic fix**: com.gftd.fleet-ci-murakumo-tick.plist's\nStandardOutPath/StandardErrorPath originally pointed at the same file the\nscript's own log! writes via appendFileSync, double-writing every line\nunder launchd (stdout redirect + explicit append). Repointed to a separate\nfleet-ci-murakumo-tick.stdout.log for raw/crash output; the structured\n.log file is the canonical record."), (:adr/decision "{:gates {kagami :jvm-test-zebulun, nekko :jvm-test-zebulun, bonsai :jvm-test-zebulun, kotoba-delta :nbb-test-asher, org-spirit-in-physics-comics :docs-check-asher}, :signer {:kagi-name \"fleet-agent-murakumo-ci\", :did \"did:key:z6MktD3itg4KnsVZZfKX2nTb19JnbzFy5WMCYbgoG4jnRNVw\", :grant \"fleet-ci/*\", :governance-authority false}, :runner {:script \"~/.gftd/run-fleet-ci-murakumo-tick.cljs\", :launchagent \"com.gftd.fleet-ci-murakumo-tick\", :interval-seconds 21600}, :not-done [:github-actions-replacement :kagitaba-item-granularity-sync :auto-advance-pin-on-green]}"), (:adr/date "2026-07-17"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/title "fleet-native CI standing runner — real gates on murakumo + narrow-scope automation key"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))